{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py::test_concurrent_processes_through_seam_both_succeed`\nintermittently fails the Gerrit Verified matrix, on changes that touch neither\n`rebar._store.gitutil` nor the test:\n\n- run 31290743251, ubuntu py3.12 — `AssertionError: writer beta failed`\n- run 31349549323, ubuntu py3.13 — `AssertionError: writer alpha failed`\n\n## ROOT CAUSE — PROVEN (test design; reproduced deterministically)\n\n**The failing inner command is `git commit`, not `git add`.** The worker is a `python -c`\nprogram whose line 9 — the line both CI tracebacks name — is the COMMIT assertion:\n\n    6  r = gitutil.run_git_write(repo, 'add', '--', f'{name}.txt')\n    7  assert r.returncode == 0, r.stderr\n    8  r = gitutil.run_git_write(repo, 'commit', '-q', '--no-verify', '-m', name)\n    9  assert r.returncode == 0, r.stderr\n\nBoth CI failures carry a **message-less** `AssertionError`, i.e. `r.stderr` was empty.\n\n`_with_index_lock_retry` takes the per-store advisory lock around **each** `run_git_write`\ncall, but the worker's add and commit are two separate calls — the PAIR is not serialized. So\nthis interleaving is legal and occurs under load:\n\n    alpha: add alpha.txt   -> index holds alpha.txt\n    beta:  add beta.txt    -> index holds alpha.txt AND beta.txt\n    alpha: commit          -> a bare `git commit` commits the WHOLE index (both files)\n    beta:  commit          -> nothing staged -> \"nothing to commit\" -> rc=1\n\n`git commit -q` writes \"nothing to commit, working tree clean\" to **stdout** and leaves\n**stderr empty** — exactly the empty-stderr rc=1 signature seen in CI.\n\nDeterministic reproduction, forcing that interleaving through the real seam:\n\n    alpha add rc=0 / beta add rc=0 / alpha commit rc=0 / beta commit rc=1\n    beta commit stderr=''\n    beta commit stdout='On branch main\\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\\n'\n    git log: alpha, seed        alpha in log: True   beta in log: False\n    HEAD contents: alpha.txt | 1 +   beta.txt | 1 +\n\nalpha's commit **swept up beta.txt**: both writers' data lands and reachability is preserved —\nonly beta's *commit* is a no-op. The test asserts `cp.returncode == 0` for both writers, which\nasserts something the product never promised: that two bare whole-index commits against one\nrepository are both non-empty. The test also flakes locally at roughly 1 in 25-65 runs.\n\nRULED OUT:\n- **Retry classification / exhaustion** — rc=1 with empty stderr never reaches\n  `_augment_lock_exhaustion`; no lock signature was involved at all.\n- **Runner resource exhaustion** — all failing job logs across the cited runs grep clean for\n  `No space` / `ENOSPC` / `Cannot allocate` / runner warnings (zero hits).\n- **A product contention defect** — every git invocation through the seam behaved correctly,\n  and git correctly reports an empty commit.\n\n## Plan\n\nTwo test-only changes, in the order the acceptance criteria require:\n\n1. **Observability first.** Each worker assertion reports only `r.stderr`, discarding both the\n   git stdout that carries the diagnosis and the identity of the failing inner command. Make\n   each assertion name its command and include stdout as well as stderr, so any future failure\n   is self-diagnosing instead of a bare `AssertionError`.\n2. **Remove the shared-index race.** Give each writer a commit that is non-empty regardless of\n   interleaving, by committing its own pathspec rather than the whole index. This preserves the\n   real oracle — two concurrent writers through `run_git_write` against one repository both\n   succeed and both commits land — without weakening it.\n\nNo file under `src/rebar/` changes: the production contention policy is correct as proven above.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A failing worker reports which inner git command failed.\n- [ ] A failing worker reports git's stdout as well as its stderr, so an empty-stderr failure\n      such as \"nothing to commit\" is diagnosable from the CI log alone.\n- [ ] Each writer commits its own path, so a writer that loses the add/commit interleaving\n      still has its own change to commit and does not observe \"nothing to commit\".\n- [ ] The test still requires that BOTH concurrent writers exit 0 through `run_git_write`.\n- [ ] The test still requires that BOTH commits are present in `git log`.\n- [ ] The test passes repeatedly under load locally (>= 60 consecutive runs, and under `-n 4`\n      xdist).\n- [ ] No file under `src/rebar/` is modified by this change."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786501275178450001,"uuid":"bedb877f-ca7b-4ae7-8caf-6586a32a99fe"}